{"name":"Shade-Grown","hex":"#4e5147","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Darkness where light, particularly sunlight, is blocked.","Something that blocks light, particularly in a window."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shield (someone or something) from light.","To shield oneself from light."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shade"},{"term":"grown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past participle of grow"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Covered by growth; overgrown.","Of a person: adult."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shade-grown coffee","blocks":[{"text":"Shade-grown coffee is a form of crop produced from coffee plants grown under a canopy of trees.A canopy of assorted types of shade trees is created to cultivate shade-grown coffee. This method allows shade-grown coffee systems to mimic natural forest conditions, and also promotes ecological interactions. Increased canopy cover in coffee systems has been shown to enhance biodiversity and support conservation efforts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Shade_grown_coffee_in_Guatemala.jpg/330px-Shade_grown_coffee_in_Guatemala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shade-grown_coffee","wikidata":"Q2122177"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Canopy_of_a_traditional_shade_coffee_plantation_in_Guatemala.jpg/500px-Canopy_of_a_traditional_shade_coffee_plantation_in_Guatemala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Canopy_of_a_traditional_shade_coffee_plantation_in_Guatemala.jpg/500px-Canopy_of_a_traditional_shade_coffee_plantation_in_Guatemala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn